WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.733
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Sarah. Welcome to Online A one, Book three.

2
00:00:06.033 --> 00:00:09.095
Hi! I'm Rithy. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.395 --> 00:00:14.891
Unit one: My Neighborhood. In this unit, you will talk about the places near your home.

4
00:00:15.883 --> 00:00:16.699
Neighbor.

5
00:00:17.399 --> 00:00:20.164
Neighbor means a person who lives near you.

6
00:00:20.464 --> 00:00:22.743
My neighbor waves to me every morning.

7
00:00:23.443 --> 00:00:26.107
Your turn. Say: Neighbor.

8
00:00:28.807 --> 00:00:29.552
Neighbor.

9
00:00:30.550 --> 00:00:31.400
Street.

10
00:00:32.100 --> 00:00:35.145
Street means a road in a town with houses or shops.

11
00:00:35.445 --> 00:00:37.154
I live on a quiet street.

12
00:00:37.854 --> 00:00:40.448
Your turn. Say: Street.

13
00:00:43.148 --> 00:00:43.789
Street.

14
00:00:44.783 --> 00:00:45.587
Corner.

15
00:00:46.287 --> 00:00:48.914
Corner means the place where two streets meet.

16
00:00:49.214 --> 00:00:51.062
There is a shop on the corner.

17
00:00:51.762 --> 00:00:54.252
Your turn. Say: Corner.

18
00:00:56.952 --> 00:00:57.640
Corner.

19
00:00:58.650 --> 00:00:59.570
Nearby.

20
00:01:00.270 --> 00:01:02.711
Nearby means not far away.

21
00:01:03.011 --> 00:01:04.650
The market is nearby.

22
00:01:05.350 --> 00:01:08.153
Your turn. Say: Nearby.

23
00:01:10.853 --> 00:01:11.762
Nearby.

24
00:01:12.750 --> 00:01:13.809
Sidewalk.

25
00:01:14.509 --> 00:01:17.786
Sidewalk means the path for people at the side of a street.

26
00:01:18.086 --> 00:01:19.725
We walk on the sidewalk.

27
00:01:20.425 --> 00:01:23.008
Your turn. Say: Sidewalk.

28
00:01:25.708 --> 00:01:26.756
Sidewalk.

29
00:01:27.750 --> 00:01:28.612
Traffic.

30
00:01:29.312 --> 00:01:32.484
Traffic means the cars and motorbikes on a road.

31
00:01:32.784 --> 00:01:35.004
There is a lot of traffic in the morning.

32
00:01:35.704 --> 00:01:38.542
Your turn. Say: Traffic.

33
00:01:41.242 --> 00:01:41.999
Traffic.

34
00:01:42.983 --> 00:01:43.775
Alley.

35
00:01:44.475 --> 00:01:48.158
Alley means a very small, narrow street.

36
00:01:48.458 --> 00:01:50.284
Cats sleep in the alley.

37
00:01:50.984 --> 00:01:53.868
Your turn. Say: Alley.

38
00:01:56.568 --> 00:01:57.360
Alley.

39
00:01:58.350 --> 00:01:59.316
Crossroad.

40
00:02:00.016 --> 00:02:03.084
Crossroad means the place where two roads cross.

41
00:02:03.384 --> 00:02:05.209
Stop at the crossroad.

42
00:02:05.909 --> 00:02:09.340
Your turn. Say: Crossroad.

43
00:02:12.040 --> 00:02:13.017
Crossroad.

44
00:02:14.017 --> 00:02:14.774
Block.

45
00:02:15.474 --> 00:02:18.553
Block means a group of buildings between streets.

46
00:02:18.853 --> 00:02:20.888
The school is one block away.

47
00:02:21.588 --> 00:02:24.043
Your turn. Say: Block.

48
00:02:26.743 --> 00:02:27.511
Block.

49
00:02:28.517 --> 00:02:29.436
Fence.

50
00:02:30.136 --> 00:02:33.761
Fence means a wall of wood or metal around a garden.

51
00:02:34.061 --> 00:02:35.364
Our fence is green.

52
00:02:36.064 --> 00:02:38.566
Your turn. Say: Fence.

53
00:02:41.266 --> 00:02:42.046
Fence.

54
00:02:43.050 --> 00:02:43.796
Gate.

55
00:02:44.496 --> 00:02:46.565
Gate means a door in a fence or wall.

56
00:02:46.865 --> 00:02:48.377
Please close the gate.

57
00:02:49.077 --> 00:02:51.578
Your turn. Say: Gate.

58
00:02:54.278 --> 00:02:55.001
Gate.

59
00:02:56.017 --> 00:02:56.797
Yard.

60
00:02:57.497 --> 00:02:59.857
Yard means the land around a house.

61
00:03:00.157 --> 00:03:01.947
My brother plays in the yard.

62
00:03:02.647 --> 00:03:05.346
Your turn. Say: Yard.

63
00:03:08.046 --> 00:03:08.815
Yard.

64
00:03:09.817 --> 00:03:12.048
Now let's listen to a conversation.

65
00:03:12.348 --> 00:03:14.603
Rithy, what is near your house?

66
00:03:15.917 --> 00:03:18.067
There is a small shop on the corner.

67
00:03:19.383 --> 00:03:21.046
Is there a lot of traffic?

68
00:03:22.350 --> 00:03:24.872
Yes, there is a lot of traffic in the morning.

69
00:03:26.183 --> 00:03:27.707
Who lives next to you?

70
00:03:29.017 --> 00:03:32.415
My neighbor, Mrs. Dara. She is very friendly!

71
00:03:33.717 --> 00:03:36.610
Grammar focus: There is and There are.

72
00:03:36.910 --> 00:03:38.550
There is a shop on the corner.

73
00:03:38.850 --> 00:03:40.768
There are many houses nearby.

74
00:03:41.068 --> 00:03:44.716
Use 'there is' for one thing and 'there are' for two or more things.

75
00:03:45.717 --> 00:03:48.323
Now read and listen. My Street.

76
00:03:48.623 --> 00:03:51.795
My name is Rithy, and I live on a busy street.

77
00:03:53.083 --> 00:03:55.280
My neighbor lives in the house on the corner.

78
00:03:56.583 --> 00:04:00.266
There is a market nearby, and there are two cafés on our block.

79
00:04:01.550 --> 00:04:05.825
There is a lot of traffic in the morning, so I walk on the sidewalk.

80
00:04:07.117 --> 00:04:11.450
Our house has a green fence, a big gate and a small yard.

81
00:04:12.750 --> 00:04:15.460
Quiz time! Choose the correct answer.

82
00:04:15.760 --> 00:04:17.563
There blank a shop on the corner.

83
00:04:17.863 --> 00:04:20.877
A, is. B, are. C, am.

84
00:04:24.883 --> 00:04:26.558
The answer is A: is.

85
00:04:28.050 --> 00:04:30.142
There blank many houses nearby.

86
00:04:30.442 --> 00:04:33.364
A, is. B, are. C, be.

87
00:04:37.350 --> 00:04:39.454
The answer is B: are.

88
00:04:40.950 --> 00:04:43.344
A person who lives near you is your blank.

89
00:04:43.644 --> 00:04:47.785
A, teacher. B, neighbor. C, cousin.

90
00:04:51.783 --> 00:04:54.387
The answer is B: neighbor.

91
00:04:55.883 --> 00:04:59.139
Now it's your turn to speak. Describe your neighborhood.

92
00:05:04.439 --> 00:05:10.505
There is a small market near my house. There are many trees on my street, and my neighbors are very friendly.

93
00:05:10.805 --> 00:05:12.352
Excellent answer, Rithy!

94
00:05:13.350 --> 00:05:18.591
Great work today! You learned twelve new words and there is and there are.

95
00:05:18.891 --> 00:05:23.343
Today's value is friendliness. Smile and say hello to everyone.

96
00:05:23.643 --> 00:05:25.947
See you in Unit two. Goodbye!

97
00:05:26.247 --> 00:05:29.794
Thank you, Ms. Sarah! Bye, everyone!

